<?xml version="1.0" ?>

<!--
  Gravity loading of a polyhedral field model, lowest-order mixed virtual element method,
  saddle point form. Companion of industrial3Gravity_fem.xml on the same mesh.

  Boundary conditions
    lateral boundary : horizontal displacement restrained, vertical free
    bottom (z=-2400) : vertical displacement restrained, horizontal free
    top (z=0)        : sigma.n = 0, the default for a face carrying no specification
    body force       : self weight through gravityVector and the material density

  The conditions match industrial3Gravity_fem.xml component for component. Displacement is
  natural in the mixed form, so a restrained component only loads the right hand side while
  the traction of the remaining components stays free, which is exactly a roller.

  This mesh carries two dimensional cells, so the boundary is named rather than selected
  geometrically. Surface 12 is the flat bottom at z = -2400, surface 2 is the flat top at
  z = 0, surfaces 4, 5, 8 and 13 are internal horizons, 6 and 7 are the two faults, and
  1, 3, 9, 10, 11, 14 and 15 are the lateral boundary. That was checked against the mesh.

  One caveat on the lateral boundary. The three constant traction modes of a face are the
  global Cartesian directions, so restraining a component is exact for them, but the three
  first moment modes follow the frame of the face: one is tangential and two are normal. Each
  is treated as prescribed only when its own direction is spanned by the unrestrained axes.
  The bottom is planar with a vertical normal, so its roller is exact. The lateral boundary is
  not axis aligned, its normals run at angles such as (0.55, 0.83, 0), so neither the tangents
  nor the normal is spanned and the first moment modes fall back to free: the lateral roller
  holds in its constant part only. The finite element file carries the same limitation in a
  different guise, since it restrains Cartesian components on an oblique face as well.

  Size. 516,027 cells and 1,200,400 faces, so this system carries 6 x 1,200,400 +
  6 x 516,027 = 10,298,562 unknowns, and it is indefinite. At the measured cost of the saddle
  point form that is on the order of 50 GB. A direct solve is out of the question at this size
  and the multigrid reduction is not yet efficient here.

  Parallel. Twelve cell arrays of this mesh contain NaN: porosity, permeability,
  initialPressure, temperature, PORO, PERMX, PERMY, PERMZ, NTG, PORO_NET, PERMX_NET and
  PERMY_NET. None is read by this problem, but in parallel the redistribution asks VTK for
  their range, which raises a floating point exception. Serial never redistributes and never
  sees them. Strip those arrays from the file before running on more than one rank.
-->
<Problem>

  <Solvers
    gravityVector="{ 0.0, 0.0, -9.8 }">
    <SolidMechanicsMixedVEM
      name="gravitySolver"
      discretization="mixedVEM1"
      targetRegions="{ Domain }"
      logLevel="1">
      <NonlinearSolverParameters
        newtonTol="1.0e-3"
        newtonMaxIter="5"/>
      <LinearSolverParameters
        solverType="gmres"
        preconditionerType="mgr"
        krylovTol="1.0e-5"
        krylovMaxIter="1000"
        logLevel="1"/>
    </SolidMechanicsMixedVEM>
  </Solvers>

  <NumericalMethods>
    <MixedVEM>
      <MixedVEMDiscretization
        name="mixedVEM1"
        hybridization="0"/>
    </MixedVEM>
  </NumericalMethods>

  <Mesh>
    <VTKMesh
      name="mesh1"
      logLevel="1"
      regionAttribute="region"
      partitionMethod="parmetis"
      partitionRefinement="1"
      file="./industrial_3.vtu"/>
  </Mesh>

  <ElementRegions>
    <CellElementRegion
      name="Domain"
      cellBlocks="{ * }"
      materialList="{ rock }"/>
  </ElementRegions>

  <Constitutive>
    <ElasticIsotropic
      name="rock"
      defaultDensity="2400"
      defaultBulkModulus="5.5556e9"
      defaultShearModulus="4.16667e9"/>
  </Constitutive>

  <FieldSpecifications>
    <!-- a prescribed displacement component is natural here: it only loads the right hand
         side, the traction of the complementary components stays free -->
    <FieldSpecification
      name="lateralX"
      objectPath="faceManager"
      fieldName="displacementTrace"
      component="0"
      scale="0.0"
      setNames="{ 1, 3, 9, 10, 11, 14, 15 }"/>

    <FieldSpecification
      name="lateralY"
      objectPath="faceManager"
      fieldName="displacementTrace"
      component="1"
      scale="0.0"
      setNames="{ 1, 3, 9, 10, 11, 14, 15 }"/>

    <FieldSpecification
      name="bottomZ"
      objectPath="faceManager"
      fieldName="displacementTrace"
      component="2"
      scale="0.0"
      setNames="{ 12 }"/>
  </FieldSpecifications>

  <Events
    maxTime="1.0">
    <PeriodicEvent
      name="solverApplications"
      forceDt="1.0"
      target="/Solvers/gravitySolver"/>

    <PeriodicEvent
      name="outputs"
      timeFrequency="1.0"
      target="/Outputs/vtkOutput"/>
  </Events>

  <Outputs>
    <VTK
      name="vtkOutput"/>
  </Outputs>

</Problem>
